"Mathematics|Honours|5|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ Mathematics — Sem 5 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Repeats across years point at the high-weight units for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">Mathematics Sem 5</b> — work the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('Mathematics','5','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> against the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('Mathematics','5','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a> and they show up quickly.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Mathematics at Delhi University is proof- and problem-driven from the first semester. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme lists Sem 1 DSCs as Algebra (UPC 2352011101, 3T+1T), Elementary Real Analysis (2352011102, 3T+1T) and Probability and Statistics (2352011103, 3T+1P). Later semesters build through Linear Algebra, Calculus, Group Theory, Riemann Integration, Multivariate Calculus and Complex Analysis. Students often lose marks by skipping rigorous steps, notation and justification that examiners score in proofs and by leaving numerical work incomplete.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
