"B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology|Honours|6|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.75;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology — Sem 6 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Solve the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology','6','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology Sem 6</b> unit-wise with the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology','6','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a> open — the pattern of repeats is the study list.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology at Delhi University starts with non-chordates and cell biology and progresses to physiology, genetics and biotechnology. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme lists Sem 1 DSCs as Nonchordata – Protists to Pseudocoelomates (UPC 2232011101), Biology of Cell: Structure and Function (2232013502) and Concept of Ecology (2232012303), each 4 credits (2 theory + 2 practical). Sem 2-4 then cover Coelomates, Human Physiology, Diversity of Chordates, Biochemistry and Developmental Biology. Students often lose marks on labelled diagrams, classification characters and practical spotting where neatness, correct terminology and original observation are scored.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology|Honours|7|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology — Sem 7 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\"><b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology Sem 7</b> revision order: map each past question to a unit with the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology','7','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a>, then revise the units that repeat most.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology at Delhi University starts with non-chordates and cell biology and progresses to physiology, genetics and biotechnology. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme lists Sem 1 DSCs as Nonchordata – Protists to Pseudocoelomates (UPC 2232011101), Biology of Cell: Structure and Function (2232013502) and Concept of Ecology (2232012303), each 4 credits (2 theory + 2 practical). Sem 2-4 then cover Coelomates, Human Physiology, Diversity of Chordates, Biochemistry and Developmental Biology. Students often lose marks on labelled diagrams, classification characters and practical spotting where neatness, correct terminology and original observation are scored.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology|Honours|8|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology — Sem 8 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Repeats across years point at the high-weight units for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology Sem 8</b> — work the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology','8','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> against the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology','8','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a> and they show up quickly.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Zoology at Delhi University starts with non-chordates and cell biology and progresses to physiology, genetics and biotechnology. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme lists Sem 1 DSCs as Nonchordata – Protists to Pseudocoelomates (UPC 2232011101), Biology of Cell: Structure and Function (2232013502) and Concept of Ecology (2232012303), each 4 credits (2 theory + 2 practical). Sem 2-4 then cover Coelomates, Human Physiology, Diversity of Chordates, Biochemistry and Developmental Biology. Students often lose marks on labelled diagrams, classification characters and practical spotting where neatness, correct terminology and original observation are scored.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Botany|Honours|2|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.75;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Botany — Sem 2 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Solve one <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Botany','2','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> paper per unit for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Botany Sem 2</b> and note which units reappear; that gives you the study order without guesswork.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Botany at Delhi University progresses from plant diversity and cell structure to systematics, ecology, physiology and biotechnology. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme lists 18 DSCs across six semesters; Sem 1 opens with Plant Diversity and Evolution (BOT-DSC-1, UPC 2162011101), Cell Biology: Organelles and Biomolecules (BOT-DSC-2, 2162011102) and Basic Laboratory and Field Skills in Plant Biology (2162011103), each 4 credits with a 2-theory + 2-practical split. Later semesters cover Phycology, Bryophytes-Pteridophytes-Gymnosperms, Genetics, Mycology, Ecology and Molecular Biology. Students often lose marks on practical records, herbarium preparation and labelled diagrams where original observation and correct nomenclature matter more than memorised text.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
