"B.Sc. (Hons) Botany|Honours|8|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Botany — Sem 8 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Repeats across years point at the high-weight units for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Botany Sem 8</b> — work the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Botany','8','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> against the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Botany','8','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a> and they show up quickly.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Botany at Delhi University progresses from plant diversity and cell structure to systematics, ecology, physiology and biotechnology. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme lists 18 DSCs across six semesters; Sem 1 opens with Plant Diversity and Evolution (BOT-DSC-1, UPC 2162011101), Cell Biology: Organelles and Biomolecules (BOT-DSC-2, 2162011102) and Basic Laboratory and Field Skills in Plant Biology (2162011103), each 4 credits with a 2-theory + 2-practical split. Later semesters cover Phycology, Bryophytes-Pteridophytes-Gymnosperms, Genetics, Mycology, Ecology and Molecular Biology. Students often lose marks on practical records, herbarium preparation and labelled diagrams where original observation and correct nomenclature matter more than memorised text.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Geology|Honours|2|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Geology — Sem 2 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Practical route for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Geology Sem 2</b>: open the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Geology','2','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a>, attempt the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Geology','2','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a>, and shortlist the units that appear in more than one paper.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Geology at Delhi University moves from earth systems and minerals to structural, igneous, palaeontological and applied geology. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 structure lists Sem 1 DSCs as Earth System Science (UPC 2192011101), Mineral Science (2192011102) and Concepts of Stratigraphy (2192011103), each 4 credits (3 theory + 1 practical). Later semesters cover Structural Geology, Igneous Petrology, Palaeontology, Sedimentary and Metamorphic Geology, Hydrogeology and Economic Geology. Students often lose marks on field-based papers — Geological Mapping (2T+2P in Sem 5) and Remote Sensing &amp; GIS — where map work, cross-sections and neat field records are assessed strictly.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
