"B.Sc. (Hons) Statistics|Honours|8|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.75;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Statistics — Sem 8 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\"><b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Statistics Sem 8</b> revision order: map each past question to a unit with the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Statistics','8','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a>, then revise the units that repeat most.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Statistics at Delhi University blends probability theory, statistical methods and mathematics from the first semester. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme lists Sem 1 DSCs as Descriptive Statistics (UPC 2372011101), Introduction to Probability (2372011102) and Calculus (2372011103), each 4 credits (3 theory + 1 practical). Sem 2-3 move to Probability Distributions, Applied Statistics and Sample Surveys, while Sem 5-6 cover Estimation, Linear Models, Testing, Design and Econometrics. Students often lose marks on derivations of distributions, correct use of formulae and interpretation of practical outputs where examiners expect stepwise working and proper notation.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology|Honours|2|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology — Sem 2 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Work through the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology','2','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> alongside the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology','2','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a> for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology Sem 2</b> — two papers are usually enough to see which units carry the marks.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology at Delhi University applies chemistry, microbiology and engineering to food processing, preservation and safety. As of 2026, the notified UGCF 2022 syllabi for Semesters 4-6 (DU notification dated 04.01.2024, Appendix-II-A, Ordinance V (2-A)) include DSC FT10 Food Quality Management as a 4-credit paper (3 theory + 1 practical) with three theory units: Introduction to Food Quality, Approaches to Food Quality Management, and Food Quality Management during production. The programme also runs through Fundamentals of Food Technology in Sem 1 to Technology of Food Preservation, Fruits-Vegetables and Dairy-Seafood (Sem 2-3) and onward to Food Engineering and Food Chemistry. Students often lose marks when they neglect precise practical protocols — HACCP plans, quality inspection of grains/pulses, and sensory evaluation sheets — where examiners check steps, not just conclusions.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology|Honours|3|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.75;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology — Sem 3 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">The quickest priority list for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology Sem 3</b>: mark the units that repeat across two <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology','3','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> papers, then revise in that order.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology at Delhi University applies chemistry, microbiology and engineering to food processing, preservation and safety. As of 2026, the notified UGCF 2022 syllabi for Semesters 4-6 (DU notification dated 04.01.2024, Appendix-II-A, Ordinance V (2-A)) include DSC FT10 Food Quality Management as a 4-credit paper (3 theory + 1 practical) with three theory units: Introduction to Food Quality, Approaches to Food Quality Management, and Food Quality Management during production. The programme also runs through Fundamentals of Food Technology in Sem 1 to Technology of Food Preservation, Fruits-Vegetables and Dairy-Seafood (Sem 2-3) and onward to Food Engineering and Food Chemistry. Students often lose marks when they neglect precise practical protocols — HACCP plans, quality inspection of grains/pulses, and sensory evaluation sheets — where examiners check steps, not just conclusions.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology|Honours|4|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology — Sem 4 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Start from the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology','4','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a> and the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology','4','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology Sem 4</b> — solve two past papers unit-wise and the repeat pattern becomes your priority list.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology at Delhi University applies chemistry, microbiology and engineering to food processing, preservation and safety. As of 2026, the notified UGCF 2022 syllabi for Semesters 4-6 (DU notification dated 04.01.2024, Appendix-II-A, Ordinance V (2-A)) include DSC FT10 Food Quality Management as a 4-credit paper (3 theory + 1 practical) with three theory units: Introduction to Food Quality, Approaches to Food Quality Management, and Food Quality Management during production. The programme also runs through Fundamentals of Food Technology in Sem 1 to Technology of Food Preservation, Fruits-Vegetables and Dairy-Seafood (Sem 2-3) and onward to Food Engineering and Food Chemistry. Students often lose marks when they neglect precise practical protocols — HACCP plans, quality inspection of grains/pulses, and sensory evaluation sheets — where examiners check steps, not just conclusions.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
