"B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology|Honours|8|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.75;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology — Sem 8 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\"><b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology Sem 8</b> revision order: map each past question to a unit with the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology','8','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a>, then revise the units that repeat most.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Food Technology at Delhi University applies chemistry, microbiology and engineering to food processing, preservation and safety. As of 2026, the notified UGCF 2022 syllabi for Semesters 4-6 (DU notification dated 04.01.2024, Appendix-II-A, Ordinance V (2-A)) include DSC FT10 Food Quality Management as a 4-credit paper (3 theory + 1 practical) with three theory units: Introduction to Food Quality, Approaches to Food Quality Management, and Food Quality Management during production. The programme also runs through Fundamentals of Food Technology in Sem 1 to Technology of Food Preservation, Fruits-Vegetables and Dairy-Seafood (Sem 2-3) and onward to Food Engineering and Food Chemistry. Students often lose marks when they neglect precise practical protocols — HACCP plans, quality inspection of grains/pulses, and sensory evaluation sheets — where examiners check steps, not just conclusions.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science|Honours|2|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science — Sem 2 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">The quickest priority list for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science Sem 2</b>: mark the units that repeat across two <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science','2','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> papers, then revise in that order.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science at Delhi University is code-heavy from the first semester and builds toward systems and AI. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 structure lists Sem 1 DSCs as Object Oriented Programming using Python (UPC 2342011104), Computer System Architecture (2342011102) and Mathematics for Computing (2342011103), each 4 credits (3 theory + 1 practical). Sem 2-4 continue with C++, Discrete Structures, Data Structures, Operating Systems, Algorithms, DBMS and Computer Networks, while Sem 5-6 add Machine Learning, Theory of Computation and Deep Learning. Students tend to lose marks when they skip practical file correctness, time complexity analysis or precise definitions that examiners expect verbatim.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
