"B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science|Honours|8|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.75;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science — Sem 8 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Solve the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science','8','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science Sem 8</b> unit-wise with the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science','8','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a> open — the pattern of repeats is the study list.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science at Delhi University is code-heavy from the first semester and builds toward systems and AI. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 structure lists Sem 1 DSCs as Object Oriented Programming using Python (UPC 2342011104), Computer System Architecture (2342011102) and Mathematics for Computing (2342011103), each 4 credits (3 theory + 1 practical). Sem 2-4 continue with C++, Discrete Structures, Data Structures, Operating Systems, Algorithms, DBMS and Computer Networks, while Sem 5-6 add Machine Learning, Theory of Computation and Deep Learning. Students tend to lose marks when they skip practical file correctness, time complexity analysis or precise definitions that examiners expect verbatim.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences|Honours|2|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences — Sem 2 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Practical route for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences Sem 2</b>: open the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences','2','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a>, attempt the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences','2','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a>, and shortlist the units that appear in more than one paper.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences at Delhi University is an integrated life-sciences degree that combines botany, zoology and chemistry rather than a single discipline. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme structure lists Sem 1 DSCs as Basic concepts of Biomolecules (UPC 6792011101), Photobiology (6792011102) and Diversity in Life forms I (6792011103), each 4 credits with a 2-theory + 2-practical split. The course then moves through Cell Biology and Diversity of Life Forms-II in Sem 2 to Functional Ecology, Metabolism, Physiology and later Molecular Biology and Evolution in Sem 5-6. Students typically find it demanding because three streams are examined together and lose marks when they treat practicals — specimen identification, biomolecule tests and field observations — as secondary to theory.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences|Honours|3|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.75;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences — Sem 3 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\">Repeats across years point at the high-weight units for <b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences Sem 3</b> — work the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences','3','pyqs');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--blue); font-weight:600;\">PYQs</a> against the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences','3','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a> and they show up quickly.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences at Delhi University is an integrated life-sciences degree that combines botany, zoology and chemistry rather than a single discipline. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme structure lists Sem 1 DSCs as Basic concepts of Biomolecules (UPC 6792011101), Photobiology (6792011102) and Diversity in Life forms I (6792011103), each 4 credits with a 2-theory + 2-practical split. The course then moves through Cell Biology and Diversity of Life Forms-II in Sem 2 to Functional Ecology, Metabolism, Physiology and later Molecular Biology and Evolution in Sem 5-6. Students typically find it demanding because three streams are examined together and lose marks when they treat practicals — specimen identification, biomolecule tests and field observations — as secondary to theory.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
"B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences|Honours|4|imp": "\n      <div style=\"background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; line-height:1.7;\">\n        <div style=\"font-family:'Sora',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:14px; margin-bottom:10px;\">⭐ B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences — Sem 4 — Important Questions <span style=\"font-weight:500; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px;\">· Verified overview — based on official syllabus</span></div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:10px;\"><b style=\"color:var(--text);\">B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences Sem 4</b> revision order: map each past question to a unit with the <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"openCoreCategory('B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences','4','syllabus');return false;\" style=\"color:var(--green); font-weight:600;\">syllabus</a>, then revise the units that repeat most.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text); line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:8px;\">B.Sc. (Hons) Biological Sciences at Delhi University is an integrated life-sciences degree that combines botany, zoology and chemistry rather than a single discipline. As of 2026, the UGCF 2022 programme structure lists Sem 1 DSCs as Basic concepts of Biomolecules (UPC 6792011101), Photobiology (6792011102) and Diversity in Life forms I (6792011103), each 4 credits with a 2-theory + 2-practical split. The course then moves through Cell Biology and Diversity of Life Forms-II in Sem 2 to Functional Ecology, Metabolism, Physiology and later Molecular Biology and Evolution in Sem 5-6. Students typically find it demanding because three streams are examined together and lose marks when they treat practicals — specimen identification, biomolecule tests and field observations — as secondary to theory.</p>\n        </div>\n    ",
